<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 59,685 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 59,685 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 59,685 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 103,693 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 5,583	   21,352</p>
<p>    Import cargo			54,102	   82,341</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, 11 ships were expected to sail and nine were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    27,000	 Chilham Castle    12/1</p>
<p>Fuel oil		 40,000	 Trade Resolve	7/1</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    25,000	 Miraj		 13/1</p>
<p>Sugar		     2,500	 Winco Pioneer	due</p>
<p>Crude</p>
<p>oil 73,000 Johar 12/1</p>
<p>Chemical		  7,500	 Bakri Orbitor	8/1</p>
<p>High speed deisel    75,000	 Chesapeak City     due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
